}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=8$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} & =9+4+3+9+12+5+6+8 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 56 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186114751 13194139533431 17592186045585 false] [17592186115974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354038 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115974 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115974 1071 "Given a data set with $9$ data points and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{9}{x}_{i}=45,$ compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$" 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115974 1071 "Given a data set with $9$ data points and $∑_(i = 1)^(9)x_{i} = 45$, compute $x^(―)$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533431 17592186045585 false] [17592186115974 1074 "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{―}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{9}{x}_{i}=45,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 45=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115975 1068 #edb/ref 17592186114757 13194139533431 17592186045585 false] [17592186115975 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354132 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115975 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115975 1071 "Given a data set with $15$ data points and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=91,$ compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ Round your answer to one decimal place." 13194139533431 17592186045585 true] [17592186115975 1071 "Given a data set with $15$ data points and $∑_(i = 1)^